meta {
  name: Unknown class - 200 with empty results
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{newBase}}/competitions/{{compId}}/classresults?class=NoSuchClass
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  class: NoSuchClass
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  **The most dangerous behaviour in the migration.** A class that does not exist
  returns `200` with `results: []` rather than an error.

  `insertResults` ends with a `notInArray` sweep that soft-deletes every stored row
  for the class that is not in the incoming set. Fed an empty set, it would wipe the
  class — so a renamed or mistyped class silently deletes its results.

  The plan handles it in the client: an empty result set returns `null` (i.e. "not
  modified"), so the sweep never runs. The trade is deliberate — a class legitimately
  emptied by the organiser keeps stale rows, which is the safer failure.
}
